Canonical Retained-Document Streaming — S7B
===============================================================================

Status: B1 contract and S7A baseline. Streaming implementation and acceptance open.
Baseline: S7A PR #825, 34cb58ad3e676723d7161ae52906395cdfaa83c0.
Branch: codex/syntax-s7b-streaming, targeting codex/syntax-s7-document-root.

1. Ownership and scope
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

S7A completes document recognition, rule-owned recovery, typed consumers, existing
semantics, and correct edits. S7B retains parsing state as source arrives. S8
switches production consumers and removes the retiring paths. S7A obligations
stay on S7A; beginning this draft does not certify its base as complete.

One canonical grammar, recognition/recovery implementation, and typed syntax
model remain authoritative. Shared execution changes belong in the S7B diff;
S2/S3 remain frozen. Inventory coverage remains 520/539: no productions added.
No new semantics, FSM scheduling, runtime activation, production caller switch,
compatibility AST, parser library, streaming grammar, or legacy fallback.
Production machinery stays safe, deterministic, platform independent core/alloc;
I/O, transports, clocks, threads, and async scheduling remain external.

This is retained-document streaming, not constant-memory consumption. Accepted
source and syntax remain inspectable. Historical snapshots retained by callers
are counted separately from the active session's storage.

2. Lifecycle and API responsibilities
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Open -> Finishing -> Finished
Open/Finishing -> Cancelled
Open/Finishing -> Limited (explicit hard-resource outcome)

Start owns document identity, parser configuration, hard limits, and counters.
Append accepts valid UTF-8 text without final EOF. It reports accepted bytes,
progress, and compact syntax/diagnostic changes. Advance processes accepted input
under a caller-provided work allowance. NeedInput and NeedsProcessing are distinct
from syntax errors and hard limits. Empty append changes no revision or counters.

Finish declares final EOF once; advance may drain its pending bounded work.
Repeated finish preserves the same completion state/result and does not repeat
work. Finished/cancelled/limited streams reject appends with defined API errors.
Cancel stops processing, retains accepted source, and never implies final EOF.
When an append exceeds retained-source capacity, reject that append atomically;
previously accepted source remains available. Other hard limits preserve every
accepted byte, including the unparsed suffix, in the explicitly limited view.

Preview yields an explicitly provisional view of current source. Finite-prefix
recovery in that view must not mutate the live delimiter/alternative continuation.
An open clean preview never authorizes execution. Finish may change diagnostics
without changing text: cache identity includes source revision AND interpretation
state/generation. Source revision alone cannot validate open/final cached output.

For x := "hel, the live string remains unfinished. Appending lo" completes it.
Only finish commits EOF recovery for any remaining unfinished construct. Errors
already established before the frontier still receive canonical S2 recovery.

3. Canonical continuation ownership
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Recognition (NoMatch/Match/Committed) remains separate from progress
(Continue/NeedInput/NeedsProcessing/Halted). Committed recovery is not suspension.
Internal frames retain owning rule and phase, source offset, delimiter/fence
ownership, alternatives and lookahead dependencies, scanner state, event/builder
state, and cumulative resources. A parent that would lose state on unwind needs
an explicit continuation, not a restart of the growing production.

Scanners retain escapes, partial delimiter matches, CRLF state, Unicode-sensitive
boundaries, and the examined frontier. Test :, :=, ., .., ..=, -, ->, ~, and ~>
as split prefixes using canonical selection rules. Long identifiers, strings,
comments, prose, and fenced bodies cannot rescan from their opening byte on each
append. A newline, closer, or successful prefix parse alone proves no universal
commitment boundary. Heading lookbehind, brace classification, and longer-token
alternatives retain their unresolved context. Replay is allowed only where its
bound is established and counted. Completed children may remain shared while
the enclosing document/section grows.

One-shot parsing must use this same recognition/recovery implementation with
final input. Frozen S7A fixtures are an independent regression reference in
addition to differential tests against the current one-shot entry point.

4. Source, tree, and publication ownership
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Preserve TextSnapshot identity, exact bytes, sharing, logical child order,
canonical shapes, and typed access. Appends must not copy all historical pieces,
scan old chunks for each range lookup, or rebuild the complete line index.
Do not normalize newlines/Unicode. Growing child arrays and structural hashes
also require bounded persistent updates, without artificial grammar nodes.

Ordinary updates publish progress, changed regions, and diagnostic deltas with a
shared/lazy provisional view. They must not enumerate every reused node or rebuild
all indexes. Full materialization, serialization, and explicitly requested whole
source/tree traversal are separate, visibly metered export operations. Merely
moving an unconditional full parse into ordinary preview does not meet the gate.

A non-append edit may invalidate continuations and use S7A's full canonical reparse.
Invalidate suspended frames and provisional caches explicitly; establish valid
streaming state before subsequent appends. Charge that restart and its reason.
Arbitrary edits need correctness and accounting, not a sublinear guarantee.

5. Limits and deterministic accounting
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Per-call allowance yields NeedsProcessing and preserves resumable state.
Hard session limits cap retained bytes, nesting/frames, events, diagnostics,
recovery work, and total work. Chunk boundaries do not reset these limits;
rewinding speculative alternatives never refunds work. Preview/export work is
separately attributed AND included in total charged work. Repeated provisional
recovery cannot escape metering. Saturation cannot silently wrap a counter.
Hard exhaustion is Limited, never NeedInput, and cannot discard accepted source.

Instrument at the owning operation, not by inferring work from reused IDs:

- accepted source bytes; scanner/parser steps; replayed bytes/steps;
- continuation resumes; emitted events; changed tree elements;
- source and child-array bytes copied; source/index maintenance work;
- diagnostic and ordinary publication work; preview/export work;
- full-document restart count and explicit reasons;
- peak live continuation/storage usage, separate from historical snapshots.

No-limit final results must agree across streamed and one-shot execution.
At limits, require the documented bounded, lossless result and correct reporting;
different strategies need not exhaust fuel at the same byte or have equal costs.

6. B1 baseline and performance gates
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The S7A DocumentSession always calls full canonical reparse for nonempty edits.
TextSnapshot append copies the piece descriptors; range lookup walks pieces.
Reparse builds fresh syntax/indexes and reconciles the old and new trees.
The baseline driver in document_streaming_complexity exercises that real API;
it is test-only and is not a proposed streaming wrapper or implementation.

The B1 counters are PARTIAL ACCOUNTING: parser steps, events, reserved
reconciliation allowance/work, and full-document restarts exposed by S7A.
Reconciliation includes reservations, so their sum is not an exact measurement
or a lower bound on executed CPU instructions.
Source copying, scanner internals, index maintenance, and exports are not fully
instrumented yet. Do not claim end-to-end cost from these counters. B2-B4 must
replace the driver with the real lifecycle and complete the owner-level metrics.
The positive acceptance assertions intentionally fail on this S7A baseline.
No ignored tests or special passing baseline mode qualify streaming.

Test fixed chunk sizes at N, 2N, 4N, 8N for a long unfinished token, growing nested
Mech expression, and fenced body. Compare each doubling with a <=3x work bound,
allowing linear/logarithmic overhead but rejecting repeated-prefix quadratic cost.
Audit both ingestion and ingestion plus normal view publication. Test one small
append to increasingly large settled prefixes with a separately bounded cost.
All tests must verify complete accepted source, final canonical structure and
normalized diagnostics, and absence of fuel/event/recovery/diagnostic truncation.
Explicit export is measured separately. Timings support, but do not replace,
deterministic counters. These selected workload bounds are not a universal
linear-time claim about every canonical grammar/input combination.

Measured B1 baseline (nightly-2026-03-03, locked/offline, no default features):

| Family | N=64 | N=128 | N=256 | N=512 |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| string | 8910 | 23214 | 68718 | 227310 |
| nested | 33036 | 86300 | 256572 | 852092 |
| fence | 8627 | 22505 | 67757 | 228245 |
| settled | 25303 | 50455 | 100759 | 201367 |

Values sum the three exposed accounting counters, including reconciliation
reservations; they are not elapsed time or executed instruction counts. Ingestion-only and
normal-view totals agree because S7A eagerly constructs the snapshot during edits.
The settled case appends six bytes to N repeated paragraphs. All four positive
performance gates fail after completing source/equivalence and cap checks.
The exact sample/counter record is `s7b-streaming-baseline.json`. B2-B4 must add
missing accounting; this table does not certify any streaming implementation.

7. Qualification and internal checkpoints
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

B1: contract, scope/stack index, measured S7A failing performance baselines.
B2: amortized append storage and resumable scanners with accurate counters.
B3: canonical frames, alternatives, final EOF, and existing recovery integration.
B4: normal snapshots/deltas, indexes, identity, finality, edit/stream transition.
B5: full correctness/resource/complexity/consumer and CI qualification.
B6: exact-head closeout, API limits and supported bounds, S8 handoff.

Begin B2/B3 with the three different unfinished families, not only independent
terminated statements. Keep all checkpoints in this single draft PR.

Focused integration targets:

- document_streaming_lifecycle: empty append, work yield, repeat finish,
  terminal API errors, cancellation, and finality/cache transitions;
- document_streaming_equivalence: tree/tokens/flags/losslessness, normalized
  diagnostic fields, typed roles, and supported semantic consumer canaries;
- document_streaming_boundaries: operators, strings/escapes, CRLF, graphemes,
  headings/fences, comprehensions, brace/shared prefixes, late disambiguation;
- document_streaming_recovery: provisional vs live state, established errors,
  physical closer ownership, later children, and canonical final EOF recovery;
- document_streaming_resources: every hard limit, resumable allowances,
  repeated previews, accepted suffix preservation, and suspended cancellation;
- document_streaming_complexity: deterministic cumulative gates described above;
- document_incremental: append/edit/append, identity and annotation invalidation.

Short fixtures use every UTF-8 character-boundary split and selected multipart
partitions; long fixtures use deterministic random, character, line, and large
chunks. Include combining characters and joined emoji. A test-only byte adapter
buffers incomplete UTF-8 suffixes and rejects malformed bytes, exercising every
byte split without transporting bytes inside the parser. Preview tests compare
the finite-prefix canonical result AND ensure the eventual final result is
unchanged. Ignore generated IDs/English wording in structural comparisons;
verify identity continuity separately.

CI's full/base mech-syntax --tests commands execute new integration targets.
Reduced-feature explicit streaming targets are added as they exist; --lib alone
is insufficient. Run pinned nightly-2026-03-03 with locked dependencies, explicit
grammar, reduced/no-std, architecture/generator, affected native/WASM, and complete
accumulated-stack consumers. Attribute results to exact heads/merge candidates.
Do not refresh grammar rows, generated files, or certification hashes for naming.

8. Closeout and S8 handoff
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Keep S7B open until correctness, actual resumability, efficient full update cost,
explicit lifecycle/resource behavior, architecture preservation, and observed
final-head qualification all pass. Known failing acceptance cannot be relabelled.

S8 uses append/advance for arriving text, provisional views for tools, and finish
at the consumer's explicit completion boundary. Only finalized validated syntax
is handed to semantic consumers. Production migration/removal stays in S8.
